{"chunks": [{"chunk_id": "0a3c995e_p1_c0", "document_id": "0a3c995e", "document_name": "Employee Travel Policy.pdf", "page_number": 1, "section": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY", "chunk_index": 0, "text": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY\nPage 1\nSection 1. Purpose & Scope\nThis policy establishes the rules and reimbursement limits for\nuniversity personnel traveling on approved academic or official\nbusiness. All travel must receive departmental pre-approval at least\n14 days prior to departure.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "0a3c995e_p2_c0", "document_id": "0a3c995e", "document_name": "Employee Travel Policy.pdf", "page_number": 2, "section": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY", "chunk_index": 1, "text": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY\nPage 2\nSection 2. Domestic Travel & Lodging\nEmployees traveling domestically may book standard single room\naccommodations not exceeding I3,500 per night in Tier 1 cities, or\nI2,200 per night in Tier 2/3 cities. Itemized receipts are mandatory\nfor all hotel claims.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "0a3c995e_p3_c0", "document_id": "0a3c995e", "document_name": "Employee Travel Policy.pdf", "page_number": 3, "section": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY", "chunk_index": 2, "text": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY\nPage 3\nSection 3. Daily Meal Allowance (Per Diem)\nA daily subsistence per diem of I1,200 is permitted during active\ntravel days. Alcoholic beverages and personal entertainment expenses\nare strictly non-reimbursable under all circumstances.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "0a3c995e_p4_c0", "document_id": "0a3c995e", "document_name": "Employee Travel Policy.pdf", "page_number": 4, "section": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY", "chunk_index": 3, "text": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY\nPage 4\nSection 4. Travel Reimbursement Limits\nEmployees may claim travel reimbursement up to I5,000 per trip for\ndomestic travel without special provost authorization. Claims must be\nsubmitted within 30 days of the travel completion date. Any domestic\ntrip exceeding I5,000 requires prior written approval from the Dean of\nFinance."}, {"chunk_id": "0a3c995e_p4_c1", "document_id": "0a3c995e", "document_name": "Employee Travel Policy.pdf", "page_number": 4, "section": "EMPLOYEE TRAVEL POLICY", "chunk_index": 4, "text": "Any domestic\ntrip exceeding I5,000 requires prior written approval from the Dean of\nFinance.\n\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "ea3432a4_p1_c0", "document_id": "ea3432a4", "document_name": "Expense Reimbursement Policy.pdf", "page_number": 1, "section": "EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT POLICY", "chunk_index": 0, "text": "EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT POLICY\nPage 1\nSection 1. General Principles\nAll business expenses incurred on behalf of the institution must be\nordinary, reasonable, and necessary for institutional operations.\nPersonal expenditures cannot be commingled with official claims.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "ea3432a4_p2_c0", "document_id": "ea3432a4", "document_name": "Expense Reimbursement Policy.pdf", "page_number": 2, "section": "EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT POLICY", "chunk_index": 1, "text": "EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT POLICY\nPage 2\nSection 2. Documentation & Receipt Thresholds\nAll individual expense claims above I500 require an original tax\ninvoice or valid digital receipt. Small miscellaneous expenses under\nI500 may be claimed with a self-declaration voucher, subject to a\nmonthly cap of I2,000.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "ea3432a4_p3_c0", "document_id": "ea3432a4", "document_name": "Expense Reimbursement Policy.pdf", "page_number": 3, "section": "EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT POLICY", "chunk_index": 2, "text": "EXPENSE REIMBURSEMENT POLICY\nPage 3\nSection 3. Equipment and Hardware Purchases\nAll IT equipment, laptops, tablets, and software subscriptions require\npre-approval from the IT Procurement Committee regardless of cost.\nReimbursing unauthorized hardware purchases is prohibited.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "0d10cb4f_p1_c0", "document_id": "0d10cb4f", "document_name": "Information Security Policy.pdf", "page_number": 1, "section": "INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY", "chunk_index": 0, "text": "INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY\nPage 1\nSection 1. Access Control & Passwords\nAll system accounts must use multi-factor authentication (MFA).\nPasswords must contain a minimum of 12 characters including uppercase,\nlowercase, numbers, and special symbols. Passwords expire every 90\ndays.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "0d10cb4f_p2_c0", "document_id": "0d10cb4f", "document_name": "Information Security Policy.pdf", "page_number": 2, "section": "INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY", "chunk_index": 1, "text": "INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY\nPage 2\nSection 2. Credential Sharing Prohibitions\nEmployees are strictly prohibited from sharing user accounts or system\npasswords with contractors, vendors, or colleagues. Each individual\nmust possess an attributed, audited account.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "0d10cb4f_p3_c0", "document_id": "0d10cb4f", "document_name": "Information Security Policy.pdf", "page_number": 3, "section": "INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY", "chunk_index": 2, "text": "INFORMATION SECURITY POLICY\nPage 3\nSection 3. Incident Reporting Timeline\nAny suspected data breach, malware infection, or unauthorized access\nattempt must be reported to the Security Operations Center (SOC)\nwithin 2 hours of discovery. Incident logs are retained for 365 days.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "165615c0_p1_c0", "document_id": "165615c0", "document_name": "Data Protection Policy.pdf", "page_number": 1, "section": "DATA PROTECTION POLICY", "chunk_index": 0, "text": "DATA PROTECTION POLICY\nPage 1\nSection 1. Personal Identifiable Information (PII)\nStudent and faculty personal data must be encrypted in transit using\nTLS 1.3 and at rest using AES-256 encryption. Access to sensitive PII\nis restricted on a strict need-to-know basis.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}, {"chunk_id": "165615c0_p2_c0", "document_id": "165615c0", "document_name": "Data Protection Policy.pdf", "page_number": 2, "section": "DATA PROTECTION POLICY", "chunk_index": 1, "text": "DATA PROTECTION POLICY\nPage 2\nSection 2. Data Retention & Erasure\nStudent academic transcripts are permanently retained. General\nadministrative correspondence and visitor logs must be securely purged\nafter 3 years. Research project data must be archived for 5 years\npost-publication.\nCompliSure Institutional Safety & Compliance Policy Document"}], "embeddings": {"0a3c995e_p1_c0": [-0.01282418891787529, 0.012477636337280273, 0.02647179551422596, -0.035464268177747726, -0.00679420493543148, 0.0024366031866520643, 0.002483938354998827, -0.010936150327324867, 0.008658808656036854, 0.006499254610389471, 0.006697286851704121, 0.00763706723228097, -0.006232107523828745, 0.01024619396775961, 0.11388784646987915, 0.002835235558450222, 0.005503525957465172, 0.015556774102151394, 0.0006534973508678377, -0.01030712015926838, -0.016449296846985817, 0.002896135440096259, -0.017372259870171547, -0.015651987865567207, 5.3929234127281234e-05, -0.036636821925640106, -0.010514537803828716, 0.012631715275347233, 0.018148135393857956, 0.013670513406395912, -0.001881791278719902, 0.0023380075581371784, -0.000471255014417693, 0.01614481769502163, 0.03466209024190903, 0.039578866213560104, 0.016174718737602234, -0.027751494199037552, 0.019088055938482285, 0.009612073190510273, 0.0010218003299087286, 0.010191503912210464, -0.0031918357126414776, 0.018789881840348244, -0.010970302857458591, 0.002814845647662878, -0.02007887326180935, -0.023187531158328056, -0.010047080926597118, 0.03823859